{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FB3mJZsnXNf1WPWFaqkor4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JdoZf88iYunJMt45nkXuoU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-14-1800-batch-mle-per-trace-h2d\n\nReplace per-trace `main_ptrs.to_device()` calls in MLE sumcheck round evaluation with per-round bulk H2D uploads. Currently, each MLE round builds a `Vec<MainMatrixPtrs>` for every Case B trace and uploads it individually, generating ~5000 H2D copies per segment (~10K total at APC 300). nsight profiling confirms the CUDA API overhead for these small transfers (~5μs each) consumes ~25ms per segment. By concatenating all per-trace MainMatrixPtrs into a single Vec and performing one bulk `to_device()` per round, we reduce ~10K H2D copies to ~48 (24 rounds × 2 segments), saving an estimated 40-50ms on MLE Rounds at APC 300.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":898,"cache_read_input_tokens":171666,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":898},"output_tokens":53,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e33616ae-361c-4ad4-bcb1-e94f2f710e44","uuid":"7be18663-1a38-4ff5-9c7a-02b02fcb6fa4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JdoZf88iYunJMt45nkXuoU","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e33616ae-361c-4ad4-bcb1-e94f2f710e44","uuid":"3f775e48-ede2-4431-90f3-c3645438d71e","timestamp":"2026-04-14T16:12:35.153Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-14-1800-batch-mle-per-trace-h2d\n\nReplace per-trace `main_ptrs.to_device()` calls in MLE sumcheck round evaluation with per-round bulk H2D uploads. Currently, each MLE round builds a `Vec<MainMatrixPtrs>` for every Case B trace and uploads it individually, generating ~5000 H2D copies per segment (~10K total at APC 300). nsight profiling confirms the CUDA API overhead for these small transfers (~5μs each) consumes ~25ms per segment. By concatenating all per-trace MainMatrixPtrs into a single Vec and performing one bulk `to_device()` per round, we reduce ~10K H2D copies to ~48 (24 rounds × 2 segments), saving an estimated 40-50ms on MLE Rounds at APC 300.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":["-# 2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers","+# 2026-04-14-1800-batch-mle-per-trace-h2d"," ","-Replace per-round DeviceMatrix allocations in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) with pre-allocated contiguous ping-pong buffers. Currently, each MLE round allocates ~1400 new DeviceMatrix objects (one per foldable trace matrix across mat_evals and sels) and frees the previous round's ~1400 matrices, totaling ~37K cudaMallocAsync + ~37K cudaFreeAsync calls across 24 MLE rounds at APC 300. By pre-allocating two contiguous buffers (one for even rounds, one for odd) and computing per-trace offsets by halving the previous round's layout, we eliminate all per-round allocation/deallocation overhead (~15-20ms) while preserving the existing batched fold kernel.","+Replace per-trace `main_ptrs.to_device()` calls in MLE sumcheck round evaluation with per-round bulk H2D uploads. Currently, each MLE round builds a `Vec<MainMatrixPtrs>` for every Case B trace and uploads it individually, generating ~5000 H2D copies per segment (~10K total at APC 300). nsight profiling confirms the CUDA API overhead for these small transfers (~5μs each) consumes ~25ms per segment. By concatenating all per-trace MainMatrixPtrs into a single Vec and performing one bulk `to_device()` per round, we reduce ~10K H2D copies to ~48 (24 rounds × 2 segments), saving an estimated 40-50ms on MLE Rounds at APC 300."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers\n\nReplace per-round DeviceMatrix allocations in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) with pre-allocated contiguous ping-pong buffers. Currently, each MLE round allocates ~1400 new DeviceMatrix objects (one per foldable trace matrix across mat_evals and sels) and frees the previous round's ~1400 matrices, totaling ~37K cudaMallocAsync + ~37K cudaFreeAsync calls across 24 MLE rounds at APC 300. By pre-allocating two contiguous buffers (one for even rounds, one for odd) and computing per-trace offsets by halving the previous round's layout, we eliminate all per-round allocation/deallocation overhead (~15-20ms) while preserving the existing batched fold kernel.\n"}}
