{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01USzXhMG7YftpY3Nfyhdk89","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Ping-Pong MLE Fold Buffers\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate ~67K per-benchmark DeviceMatrix allocations and ~67K frees in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) by replacing them with two pre-allocated contiguous device buffers used in a ping-pong pattern. MLE Rounds at APC 300 take 173ms, of which ~15-20ms is CUDA memory pool API overhead from these allocations (confirmed by the bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers task which recovered 13ms with a heavier ArenaMatrix approach). This cleaner implementation avoids the ArenaMatrix/MatrixRef/FoldArena type complexity of the previous attempt.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### MLE Rounds loop\n10\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:631-648`\n11\t```rust\n12\tfor round in 1..=n_max {\n13\t    let sp_round_evals = prover.sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(round, r[round - 1])?;\n14\t    // ... transcript observe, sample r_round ...\n15\t    prover.fold_mle_evals(round, r_round)?;\n16\t}\n17\t```\n18\t\n19\t### fold_mle_evals\n20\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1999-2091`\n21\t\n22\tContains `batch_fold` closure (lines 2002-2048):\n23\t1. Counts foldable matrices (height > 1) via `partition_point` (line 2003)\n24\t2. Allocates output: `DeviceMatrix::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height, width)` per foldable matrix (line 2014) → `cudaMallocAsync`\n25\t3. Collects input/output pointer Vecs (lines 2019-2027)\n26\t4. Uploads 4 pointer arrays to device (lines 2029-2032)\n27\t5. Launches single `batch_fold_mle` kernel (lines 2034-2044)\n28\t6. Returns new output matrices, dropping old inputs → `cudaFreeAsync` each\n29\t\n30\tCalled twice per round:\n31\t- `mat_evals_per_trace` (lines 2050-2066): ~800 matrices at APC 300\n32\t- `sels_per_trace` (line 2078): ~623 matrices\n33\t\n34\tPer round: ~1400 allocs + ~1400 frees = ~2800 CUDA API calls.\n35\tPer benchmark (24 rounds × 2 segments): ~134K API calls (~67K allocs, ~67K frees).\n36\tAt 0.3-0.5μs per call: **20-33ms total overhead** (previous task confirmed 13ms recovery, suggesting ~15-20ms was actual overhead).\n37\t\n38\t### sumcheck_polys_batch_eval\n39\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1536-1922`\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SNvxRv37zpqBNiVKojzG8X","session_id":"e33616ae-361c-4ad4-bcb1-e94f2f710e44","uuid":"a6ba5aa0-f96d-40f6-82c1-acd0f3182874","timestamp":"2026-04-14T16:15:12.845Z"}
