pecific prime P was chosen to:\n44\t/// - Be less than 2^31 so that it fits within a 32 bit word and doesn't overflow on addition.\n45\t/// - Otherwise have as large a power of 2 in the factors of P-1 as possible.\n46\t///\n47\t/// This last property is useful for number theoretical transforms (the fast fourier transform\n48\t/// equivalent on finite fields).  See NTT.h for details.\n49\t///\n50\t/// The Fp class wraps all the standard arithmetic operations to make the finite field elements look"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018d7aaZfiYC2rMye6NqePyf","session_id":"e33616ae-361c-4ad4-bcb1-e94f2f710e44","uuid":"8ce67718-9dae-4057-a41f-1fcc6b901a94","timestamp":"2026-04-14T16:24:32.759Z"}
