{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MVidVmqCmitv5gMhtL5FyH","type":"tool_result","content":"96-            self.observe(x);\n97-        }\n98-    }\n99-}\n100-\n101-/// GPU-accelerated duplex sponge that maintains state on both host and device.\n102-///\n103-/// The host-side state uses [`DeviceSpongeState`] which matches the behavior of\n104-/ `DuplexSponge` from openvm_stark_backend (and `p3_challenger::DuplexChallenger`).\n105-/// The device-side state is stored in GPU memory for CUDA kernel operations.\n106-///\n107-/// # State Synchronization\n108-///\n109-/ The host and device states are **independent** and must be explicitly synchronized:\n110-/ - Use [`sync_h2d`](Self::sync_h2d) to copy host state to device before GPU operations\n111:/// - Use [`sync_d2h`](Self::sync_d2h) to copy device state back to host after GPU operations\n112-///\n113-/// # Usage Example\n114-///\n115-/// ```ignore\n116-/ let mut sponge = DuplexSpongeGpu::default();\n117-///\n118-/// // Do some host operations\n119-/// sponge.observe(some_value);\n120-/// let challenge = sponge.sample();\n121-///\n122-/// // Sync to device before GPU grinding\n123-/// sponge.sync_h2d()?;\n124-///\n125-/// // ... GPU grinding kernel runs ...\n126-///\n127-/// // Sync back after GPU modifies state\n128:/// sponge.sync_d2h()?;\n129-///\n130-/// // Continue with host operations\n131-/// let next_challenge = sponge.sample();\n132-/// ```\n133-#[derive(Debug)]\n134-pub struct DuplexSpongeGpu {\n135-    /// Host-side structure\n136-    host: Challenger,\n137-    /// Device-side state buffer (allocated lazily on first sync)\n138-    device: DeviceBuffer<DeviceSpongeState>,\n139-}\n140-\n141-impl Default for DuplexSpongeGpu {\n142-    fn default() -> Self {\n143-        Self::new()"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bk2X7Ug1SRvaG861UVxTFP","session_id":"e33616ae-361c-4ad4-bcb1-e94f2f710e44","uuid":"ceac7082-2b14-4e26-8832-a91cae1cfdc6","timestamp":"2026-04-14T16:29:40.655Z"}
