{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E3zJWNEkh11rsbFWhUB9Vn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: GPU-Side GKR Transcript Processing\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate per-round CPU-GPU roundtrips in the GKR fractional sumcheck by moving the `observe_and_update` function (D2H copy + arithmetic + Poseidon2 transcript observe/sample) to a GPU kernel. This targets the 14ms per-segment inter-kernel gap measured by nsight in the fractional sumcheck round loop (28ms total across 2 segments at APC 300).\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### Call chain\n10\t\n11\t```\n12\tfractional_sumcheck_gpu() @ fractional.rs:491\n13\t└─ for round in 1..total_rounds (line 655)\n14\t    ├─ eq_buffer = SqrtEqLayers::from_xi() (line 663) — CPU\n15\t    ├─ lambda = transcript.sample_ext() (line 670) — CPU Poseidon2 sponge\n16\t    ├─ do_sumcheck_round_and_revert() (line 698) — GPU kernel + observe_and_update\n17\t    └─ match backend:\n18\t         ├─ FoldEval: for xi_j { do_fused_sumcheck_round() } — GPU + observe_and_update per inner round\n19\t         └─ PrecomputeM: precompute_m → multifold → observe_and_update (with CPU eq_table deps)\n20\t```\n21\t\n22\t### Per-round observe_and_update (fractional.rs:318-346)\n23\t\n24\tEach call does:\n25\t1. **D2H sync**: `d_sum_evals.to_host()` — copies 2 EF (32 bytes) from GPU, BLOCKS until preceding GPU kernel completes\n26\t2. **CPU arithmetic**: `reconstruct_s_evals()` — ~12 EF field operations (inverse, interpolation)\n27\t3. **CPU transcript**: `transcript.observe_ext()` × 3 — absorbs 12 BabyBear elements, triggers 1-2 Poseidon2 permutations (~10μs each)\n28\t4. **CPU transcript**: `transcript.sample_ext()` — squeezes 4 BabyBear elements, triggers 0-1 Poseidon2 permutations\n29\t5. **CPU accumulator update**: `eq_r_acc *= ...`, `prev_s_eval = ...`\n30\t6. **Return**: challenge `r` used by next round's GPU kernel (passed as scalar argument)\n31\t\n32\t### Why it's slow\n33\t\n34\tnsight profiling of the fractional sumcheck kernel timeline shows:\n35\t- Segment 0: 80.5ms wall time, 14.2ms of inter-kernel gaps across ~41 major kernel transitions (mean gap: 0.35ms)\n36\t- Segment 1: 80.3ms wall time, 14.0ms of inter-kernel gaps\n37\t- Each gap is a CPU-GPU roundtrip: GPU idles while CPU does D2H + reconstruct + transcript + next kernel launch\n38\t\n39\t### Existing GPU infrastructure\n40\t\n41\t- **GPU Poseidon2 permutation**: `poseidon2_mix(Fp *cells)` in `crates/cuda-common/include/poseidon2.cuh:184-202`\n42\t- **GPU sponge functions**: `sponge_observe()` and `sponge_sample()` as `__device__` functions in `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/sponge.cu:13-42` (must be extracted to shared header)\n43\t- **DeviceSpongeState struct**: defined in both Rust (`sponge.rs:32-39`) and CUDA (`sponge.cu`), `#[repr(C)]` ABI-compatible\n44\t- **Host-device sync**: `DuplexSpongeGpu::sync_h2d()` at `sponge.rs:188` converts Challenger → DeviceSpongeState and uploads\n45\t- **FpExt arithmetic**: Extension field arithmetic already exists in CUDA for GKR kernels (`FracExt` type with multiply, add). Check `fpext.h` or equivalent for `reciprocal()`.\n46\t\n47\t## Changes\n48\t\n49\t### Scope: FoldEval path only (initial prototype)\n50\t\n51\tThe PrecomputeM path (fractional.rs:817+) uses per-round challenges in CPU-side `eval_mle_table` to build eq tables. Moving this to GPU requires additional scope (GPU-side eq table construction). The initial prototype targets the FoldEval path only. When the round strategy selects PrecomputeM, fall back to the existing CPU observe_and_update path.\n52\t\n53\t### Change 1: Extract sponge functions to shared header\n54\t\n55\t**File**: Create `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/include/sponge.cuh` (new header)\n56\t\n57\tExtract from `sponge.cu`:\n58\t- `DeviceSpongeState` struct definition\n59\t- `sponge_observe()` device function\n60\t- `sponge_sample()` device function\n61\t\n62\tUpdate `sponge.cu` to `#include \"sponge.cuh\"` and remove the inlined definitions.\n63\t\n64\t### Change 2: New CUDA kernel `gkr_round_postprocess`\n65\t\n66\t**File**: Add to `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/sumcheck.cu` (or new file)\n67\t\n68\t```cuda\n69\t#include \"sponge.cuh\"\n70\t#include \"fpext.h\"  // FpExt arithmetic\n71\t\n72\t__global__ void gkr_round_postprocess(\n73\t    const FpExt *d_sum_evals,      // 2 EF values from compute_round kernel\n74\t    DeviceSpongeState *sponge,     // transcript sponge state (modified in-place)\n75\t    FpExt *d_prev_s_eval,          // scalar accumulator\n76\t    FpExt *d_eq_r_acc,             // scalar accumulator\n77\t    FpExt xi_j,                    // constant per call (passed by value)\n78\t    FpExt *d_challenge_out,        // output: sampled challenge r\n79\t    FpExt *d_s_evals_out           // output: 3 EF for round_polys_eval\n80\t) {\n81\t    // Single thread: all work is sequential, tiny data\n82\t    FpExt eq_r_acc = *d_eq_r_acc;\n83\t    FpExt prev_s_eval = *d_prev_s_eval;\n84\t    \n85\t    // 1. Reconstruct s_evals (matches fractional.rs:1126-1163)\n86\t    FpExt sp[3];\n87\t    sp[1] = d_sum_evals[0] * eq_r_acc;\n88\t    sp[2] = d_sum_evals[1] * eq_r_acc;\n89\t    FpExt eq_xi_0 = FpExt::one() - xi_j;\n90\t    sp[0] = (prev_s_eval - xi_j * sp[1]) * reciprocal(eq_xi_0);\n91\t    \n92\t    // s(X) = eq(xi_j, X) * sp(X)\n93\t    // eq(xi_j, x) = xi_j * x + (1-xi_j) * (1-x)\n94\t    FpExt s_evals[3];\n95\t    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n96\t        FpExt x = FpExt::from_u32(i + 1);\n97\t        FpExt sp_x = (i < 2) ? sp[i + 1] : lagrange_interp_012(sp, x);\n98\t        FpExt eq_val = xi_j * x + eq_xi_0 * (FpExt::one() - x);\n99\t        s_evals[i] = eq_val * sp_x;\n100\t    }\n101\t    d_s_evals_out[0] = s_evals[0];\n102\t    d_s_evals_out[1] = s_evals[1];\n103\t    d_s_evals_out[2] = s_evals[2];\n104\t    \n105\t    // 2. Transcript observe: 3 EF = 12 F elements\n106\t    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n107\t        for (int c = 0; c < 4; c++) {\n108\t            sponge_observe(*sponge, s_evals[i].coeffs[c]);\n109\t        }\n110\t    }\n111\t    \n112\t    // 3. Transcript sample: 1 EF = 4 F elements\n113\t    FpExt r;\n114\t    for (int c = 0; c < 4; c++) {\n115\t        r.coeffs[c] = sponge_sample(*sponge);\n116\t    }\n117\t    *d_challenge_out = r;\n118\t    \n119\t    // 4. Update accumulators\n120\t    FpExt eq_r_val = xi_j * r + eq_xi_0 * (FpExt::one() - r);\n121\t    *d_eq_r_acc = eq_r_acc * eq_r_val;\n122\t    *d_prev_s_eval = eq_r_val * lagrange_interp_012(sp, r);\n123\t}\n124\t```\n125\t\n126\tAlso implement `lagrange_interp_012(FpExt vals[3], FpExt x)` as a device helper that evaluates the degree-2 Lagrange interpolation through points (0,1,2) at x.\n127\t\n128\t### Change 3: FFI binding for gkr_round_postprocess\n129\t\n130\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` (or new cuda module file)\n131\t\n132\t```rust\n133\textern \"C\" { fn _gkr_round_postprocess(...) -> i32; }\n134\t\n135\tpub unsafe fn gkr_round_postprocess(\n136\t    d_sum_evals: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n137\t    d_sponge: &DeviceBuffer<DeviceSpongeState>,\n138\t    d_prev_s_eval: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n139\t    d_eq_r_acc: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n140\t    xi_j: EF,\n141\t    d_challenge_out: *mut EF,  // pointer into pre-allocated challenge array\n142\t    d_s_evals_out: *mut EF,    // pointer into pre-allocated s_evals array\n143\t) -> Result<(), CudaError> { ... }\n144\t```\n145\t\n146\t### Change 4: Modify compute_round kernels to read challenge from device pointer\n147\t\n148\t**Files**: \n149\t- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/sumcheck.cu` — kernel signatures\n150\t- `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` — FFI wrappers\n151\t\n152\tFor `frac_compute_round_and_fold` and `frac_compute_round_and_fold_inplace`:\n153\t- Add a `const FpExt *d_r_prev` parameter (device pointer to previous round's challenge)\n154\t- At kernel start: `FpExt r_prev = *d_r_prev;` (L1 cache hit, negligible latency)\n155\t- Remove the scalar `r_prev` parameter\n156\t\n157\tKeep the existing scalar-argument versions as fallback (for PrecomputeM path and first round where challenge comes from CPU).\n158\t\n159\t### Change 5: Modify FoldEval round loop in fractional_sumcheck_gpu\n160\t\n161\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n162\t\n163\tBefore the outer round loop:\n164\t```rust\n165\t// Allocate device buffers for GPU-side transcript processing\n166\tlet d_sponge = transcript.sync_h2d()?;  // Upload current sponge state\n167\tlet d_prev_s_eval = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(1);\n168\tlet d_eq_r_acc = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(1);\n169\tlet max_inner_rounds = total_rounds;\n170\tlet d_challenges = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(max_inner_rounds * total_rounds);\n171\tlet d_s_evals_array = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(max_inner_rounds * total_rounds * 3);\n172\t```\n173\t\n174\tFor the FoldEval inner loop, replace `observe_and_update()` with:\n175\t```rust\n176\tgkr_round_postprocess(\n177\t    &d_sum_evals,\n178\t    &d_sponge,\n179\t    &d_prev_s_eval,\n180\t    &d_eq_r_acc,\n181\t    xi_j,\n182\t    d_challenges.as_mut_ptr().add(challenge_idx),\n183\t    d_s_evals_array.as_mut_ptr().add(s_eval_idx * 3),\n184\t)?;\n185\tchallenge_idx += 1;\n186\ts_eval_idx += 1;\n187\t```\n188\t\n189\tPass `d_challenges.as_ptr().add(challenge_idx - 1)` as the device pointer for the next compute_round kernel's `r_prev` argument.\n190\t\n191\tFor PrecomputeM rounds: fall back to existing `observe_and_update()` CPU path. Before the PrecomputeM block, D2H the current sponge state (`sync_d2h`) and accumulators. After PrecomputeM, re-upload (`sync_h2d`).\n192\t\n193\t### Change 6: Post-loop CPU transcript replay\n194\t\n195\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n196\t\n197\tAfter the outer round loop completes:\n198\t```rust\n199\t// D2H: retrieve all round results\n200\tlet all_s_evals = d_s_evals_array.to_host()?;  // total_inner_rounds × 3 EF\n201\tlet all_challenges = d_challenges.to_host()?;   // total_inner_rounds EF\n202\t\n203\t// Replay transcript operations on CPU to synchronize transcript state\n204\tfor i in 0..total_inner_rounds {\n205\t    let s_evals = &all_s_evals[i*3 .. (i+1)*3];\n206\t    for &eval in s_evals {\n207\t        transcript.observe_ext(eval);\n208\t    }\n209\t    let _r = transcript.sample_ext();\n210\t    // Verify: debug_assert_eq!(_r, all_challenges[i]);\n211\t}\n212\t\n213\t// Populate round_polys_eval and r_vec from D2H'd data\n214\tfor i in 0..total_inner_rounds {\n215\t    round_polys_eval.push([all_s_evals[i*3], all_s_evals[i*3+1], all_s_evals[i*3+2]]);\n216\t    r_vec.push(all_challenges[i]);\n217\t}\n218\t```\n219\t\n220\tThis avoids implementing `sync_d2h` entirely. The CPU transcript replay is cheap (~50μs for ~400 sponge operations) and guarantees the CPU transcript state is correct for subsequent phases.\n221\t\n222\tA `debug_assert_eq!` on each replayed challenge vs. the GPU-produced challenge serves as a built-in correctness check.\n223\t\n224\t### Change 7: Implement sync_h2d for DuplexSpongeGpu from fractional_sumcheck_gpu\n225\t\n226\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n227\t\n228\tThe `fractional_sumcheck_gpu` function is generic over `TS: FiatShamirTranscript<SC>`. To access `DuplexSpongeGpu::sync_h2d()`, we need to either:\n229\t\n230\t**Option A (recommended)**: Add a `d_sponge: &DeviceBuffer<DeviceSpongeState>` parameter to `fractional_sumcheck_gpu`. The caller (which has access to the concrete `DuplexSpongeGpu` type) performs the sync_h2d before calling and passes the device pointer. This avoids changing the generic signature.\n231\t\n232\t**Option B**: Add a trait bound like `TS: FiatShamirTranscript<SC> + HasDeviceSponge`. This is cleaner but changes the API surface.\n233\t\n234\tOption A is minimal: the caller at `prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu` (mod.rs:489) already has access to the DuplexSpongeGpu and can sync + pass the device buffer.\n235\t\n236\t## Invariants\n237\t\n238\t1. **Transcript determinism**: The GPU Poseidon2 sponge must produce identical results to the CPU sponge. This is verified by the debug_assert_eq on replayed challenges (Change 6). The sponge functions in `sponge.cu` use the same constants and algorithm as `poseidon2.cuh`, which matches the CPU implementation.\n239\t\n240\t2. **No protocol change**: Same challenges produced in same order. Only execution location changes.\n241\t\n242\t3. **FoldEval-only scope**: PrecomputeM rounds use the existing CPU path (with sync overhead). This ensures the optimization is safe for the initial prototype. The PrecomputeM path accounts for a minority of inner rounds (typically the last few per outer round).\n243\t\n244\t4. **Sponge state consistency**: After the GKR round loop, the CPU transcript is synchronized via replay (Change 6), not via sync_d2h. The replay produces the exact same state because the transcript is deterministic (same inputs → same outputs).\n245\t\n246\t5. **No APC 0 regression**: At APC 0, fewer GKR rounds means less overhead to eliminate. The fixed cost of buffer allocation and post-loop replay is small (~0.1ms). The optimization should be neutral-to-positive.\n247\t\n248\t## Measurement Plan\n249\t\n250\tBuild and run the standard benchmarks:\n251\t```bash\n252\tcd /home/georg/powdr/results/pairing\n253\tcargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"\n254\tPROVE_BIN=$(cargo metadata --format-version 1 --no-deps 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"target_directory\"])')/release/powdr_openvm_riscv\n255\t$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics <path>/after_apc300.json --recursion\n256\t$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics <path>/after_apc000.json --recursion\n257\t```\n258\t\n259\tAnalyze with `python3 /home/georg/spec.py <metrics_path> <name>`.\n260\t\n261\tRun nsight profiling to verify inter-kernel gap reduction:\n262\t```bash\n263\tnsys profile --output <output> --force-overwrite true --trace cuda,nvtx,osrt --sample none --stats true -- $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --recursion\n264\t```\n265\t\n266\t### Expected results\n267\t- LogUp GKR at APC 300: 526ms → ~500ms (FoldEval rounds only; ~26ms from FoldEval gaps eliminated, PrecomputeM gaps remain)\n268\t- STARK excl trace at APC 300: 1296ms → ~1270ms\n269\t- Fractional sumcheck FoldEval inter-kernel gaps: 14ms → ~3ms per segment (residual from kernel launch overhead + PrecomputeM fallback gaps)\n270\t- No regression at APC 0\n271\t- All debug_assert_eq on replayed challenges pass\n272\t\n273\t### Verification\n274\t- Proof verification must pass at APC 0, 100, and 300\n275\t- Debug assertions on GPU-vs-CPU challenge comparison must hold\n276\t\n277\t## Rollback Criteria\n278\t\n279\tRevert if:\n280\t- LogUp GKR improvement at APC 300 is less than 10ms\n281\t- Any regression at APC 0 exceeds 10ms on STARK excl trace\n282\t- Proof verification fails at any APC configuration\n283\t- GPU-produced challenges differ from CPU reference (debug_assert fires)\n284\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RAfV4P8puVUmVVW47UfM8T","session_id":"e33616ae-361c-4ad4-bcb1-e94f2f710e44","uuid":"4f1c45a1-c685-4d09-96b0-db35f0e460e6","timestamp":"2026-04-14T16:35:52.307Z"}
