{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0118EieRphx16MhhMgWyyiuU","type":"tool_result","content":"148\t    fn clone(&self) -> Self {\n149\t        let mut new = Self {\n150\t            host: self.host.clone(),\n151\t            device: DeviceBuffer::new(),\n152\t        };\n153\t        // Sync cloned host state to device if device was allocated\n154\t        if !self.device.is_empty() {\n155\t            let _ = new.sync_h2d();\n156\t        }\n157\t        new\n158\t    }\n159\t}\n160\t\n161\timpl DuplexSpongeGpu {\n162\t    /// Create a new GPU-accelerated duplex sponge with default (zeroed) state.\n163\t    pub fn new() -> Self {\n164\t        Self {\n165\t            host: Challenger::new(default_babybear_poseidon2_16()),\n166\t            device: DeviceBuffer::new(),\n167\t        }\n168\t    }\n169\t\n170\t    /// Returns true if the device buffer has been allocated.\n171\t    pub fn is_device_allocated(&self) -> bool {\n172\t        !self.device.is_empty()\n173\t    }\n174\t\n175\t    /// Ensure the device buffer is allocated.\n176\t    fn ensure_device_allocated(&mut self) {\n177\t        if self.device.is_empty() {\n178\t            self.device = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(1);\n179\t        }\n180\t    }\n181\t\n182\t    /// Synchronize state from host to device (H2D memcpy).\n183\t    ///\n184\t    /// Call this before running GPU kernels that read/modify the sponge state.\n185\t    ///\n186\t    /// This converts from `DuplexChallenger`'s representation (with buffered input/output)\n187\t    /// to `DeviceSpongeState`'s representation (with indices pointing into state).\n188\t    pub fn sync_h2d(&mut self) -> Result<(), MemCopyError> {\n189\t        self.ensure_device_allocated();\n190\t\n191\t        // Convert DuplexChallenger state to DeviceSpongeState format:\n192\t        // - DuplexChallenger buffers input values before writing to sponge_state\n193\t        // - DeviceSpongeState writes directly to state[absorb_idx]\n194\t        // We need to overlay the input_buffer onto state[0..len]\n195\t\n196\t        let mut device_state = DeviceSpongeState {\n197\t            state: self.host.sponge_state,\n198\t            absorb_idx: self.host.input_buffer.len() as u32,\n199\t            sample_idx: self.host.output_buffer.len() as u32,\n200\t        };\n201\t\n202\t        // Overlay pending input_buffer values onto the beginning of state\n203\t        // (DuplexChallenger writes to state[0..N] during duplexing, so pending\n204\t        // values that haven't been duplexed yet need to be placed there)\n205\t        for (i, &val) in self.host.input_buffer.iter().enumerate() {\n206\t            device_state.state[i] = val;\n207\t        }"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01M1j6Dim2tKqR3WQfbHLQ7u","session_id":"e33616ae-361c-4ad4-bcb1-e94f2f710e44","uuid":"5f651a61-1793-4b0c-b146-a4890bbb9bc1","timestamp":"2026-04-14T16:42:54.558Z"}
