{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CMSSQSzg8PmxYbnn2wNFpt","type":"tool_result","content":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-14-1800-gpu-gkr-transcript-processing\n\nEliminate per-round CPU-GPU roundtrips in the GKR fractional sumcheck by moving the transcript observe/sample operations to GPU. Currently, each GKR sumcheck round launches a GPU kernel, then does a blocking D2H copy of 2 field elements, CPU-side arithmetic (reconstruct_s_evals), CPU-side Poseidon2 transcript absorb/squeeze, and finally launches the next round's kernel. With ~20 rounds per segment × 2 segments = ~40 roundtrips, nsight profiling shows 14ms of inter-kernel gap per segment (28ms total) from these CPU-GPU transitions. By implementing a small GPU kernel that fuses the post-round processing (reconstruct, sponge observe, sponge squeeze, accumulator update), we eliminate all mid-loop D2H copies and keep the entire GKR round loop on the GPU, with a single D2H at the end to retrieve the final transcript state.\n\n=== plan.md exists ===\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 19440 Apr 14 18:45 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1800-gpu-gkr-transcript-processing/plan.md\n\n=== baseline exists ===\napc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\nnsys_apc300.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc300.sqlite\nsummary.md\n\n=== current metrics ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc000.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc100.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300_metrics.json\n\n=== no source code modified ===\n[rerun: b39]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e33616ae-361c-4ad4-bcb1-e94f2f710e44","uuid":"99367871-df1c-4ba9-a59d-5098e23719c3","timestamp":"2026-04-14T16:45:49.285Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-14-1800-gpu-gkr-transcript-processing\n\nEliminate per-round CPU-GPU roundtrips in the GKR fractional sumcheck by moving the transcript observe/sample operations to GPU. Currently, each GKR sumcheck round launches a GPU kernel, then does a blocking D2H copy of 2 field elements, CPU-side arithmetic (reconstruct_s_evals), CPU-side Poseidon2 transcript absorb/squeeze, and finally launches the next round's kernel. With ~20 rounds per segment × 2 segments = ~40 roundtrips, nsight profiling shows 14ms of inter-kernel gap per segment (28ms total) from these CPU-GPU transitions. By implementing a small GPU kernel that fuses the post-round processing (reconstruct, sponge observe, sponge squeeze, accumulator update), we eliminate all mid-loop D2H copies and keep the entire GKR round loop on the GPU, with a single D2H at the end to retrieve the final transcript state.\n\n=== plan.md exists ===\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 19440 Apr 14 18:45 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1800-gpu-gkr-transcript-processing/plan.md\n\n=== baseline exists ===\napc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\nnsys_apc300.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc300.sqlite\nsummary.md\n\n=== current metrics ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc000.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc100.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300_metrics.json\n\n=== no source code modified ===","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
